[{:db/id "q-8306/selection/21403d7f93c174215eda9e0ad4a5a2209b54876d1b214ffcb72f4f0cc09d2fe2" :answer/id #uuid "288e641e-7ea0-5f6b-9d5e-80cbc990c2db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-2)/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8306/selection/a0415827acf53c834f6e4f7fb681dbb3defa8fdb25726a81c547e3403bf89861" :answer/id #uuid "a856d485-ab02-5026-a011-e5af6ee3a032" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{(2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1)/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8306/selection/e905d8695c1b342e03a5222287276a942e65f12c376d50811fbf944c0f4050c7" :answer/id #uuid "d1171d0b-9306-5abf-bb3c-f63a1765d918" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8306/selection/d8fcba564c3264bf227a39ad987e6db6fde942a67524cd265dd8254f314ee811" :answer/id #uuid "aa1997e3-9970-5822-8297-752f743908e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8306/selection/04d26ba07144d26ef48d2bb1d4b132bf042d74eb1591bf44ac1254b2a793bbb4" :answer/id #uuid "d2c58674-2916-5327-9520-a966791f8e00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8306/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ddc53b5-eadc-51e8-9c3e-6f48b7070bc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8306/selection/e905d8695c1b342e03a5222287276a942e65f12c376d50811fbf944c0f4050c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-8306/selection/21403d7f93c174215eda9e0ad4a5a2209b54876d1b214ffcb72f4f0cc09d2fe2" "q-8306/selection/a0415827acf53c834f6e4f7fb681dbb3defa8fdb25726a81c547e3403bf89861" "q-8306/selection/e905d8695c1b342e03a5222287276a942e65f12c376d50811fbf944c0f4050c7" "q-8306/selection/d8fcba564c3264bf227a39ad987e6db6fde942a67524cd265dd8254f314ee811" "q-8306/selection/04d26ba07144d26ef48d2bb1d4b132bf042d74eb1591bf44ac1254b2a793bbb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8306" :question/id #uuid "177e97c5-b0fe-5fdf-abe1-80b42d3faf53" :question/math-academy-id "q-8306" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}/3} & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{4/3} & =1 \\\\ K & ={e}^{-4/3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4/3}\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8306/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8306"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8310"] :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$ that satisfies $y(1)=2.$ Assume that $x>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $x>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+C} & =2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{C} & =2 \\\\ C & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=2$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{-1}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2})}=\\frac{2}{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-104058/selection/7f3a9aa515d70614b35c5c92c0e25ca38f63c0ecf220082fd684cad58d54768e" :answer/id #uuid "13e70303-6e01-5cc5-bb94-b26acfeeebfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|+y=2{x}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104058/selection/ec6cb7081418b665584eb8de2d09d1b2ad07c3d26e190b4bbecf94c256ae22f5" :answer/id #uuid "83146c73-c536-5451-b0e3-e6238f76276e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y=2{x}^{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104058/selection/465208af1beac15a27ac7a7c29e3a7529c77da818598e64bb8e3a2cfa4041ee6" :answer/id #uuid "3499a528-3b5b-5342-a45f-58ae5606f8f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104058/selection/809b957d9db412e9669f196afdc5e98872d93f9f6f8f770be28ac4e2eb1e0b9f" :answer/id #uuid "b7b648b8-3bba-5404-bcfd-aefa9938d0b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|+y={x}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104058/selection/cd90443d08905a8f82456c8cdc9ff220b3807583490c5d4e5aa7c1f3b9f57299" :answer/id #uuid "6024ef2e-28f1-5f1a-b820-5f13c5c76835" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104058/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "921db6b7-2b72-5413-ada5-2ba6ae2de3c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104058/selection/cd90443d08905a8f82456c8cdc9ff220b3807583490c5d4e5aa7c1f3b9f57299" :answer-field/choices ["q-104058/selection/7f3a9aa515d70614b35c5c92c0e25ca38f63c0ecf220082fd684cad58d54768e" "q-104058/selection/ec6cb7081418b665584eb8de2d09d1b2ad07c3d26e190b4bbecf94c256ae22f5" "q-104058/selection/465208af1beac15a27ac7a7c29e3a7529c77da818598e64bb8e3a2cfa4041ee6" "q-104058/selection/809b957d9db412e9669f196afdc5e98872d93f9f6f8f770be28ac4e2eb1e0b9f" "q-104058/selection/cd90443d08905a8f82456c8cdc9ff220b3807583490c5d4e5aa7c1f3b9f57299"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104058" :question/id #uuid "f1428f3d-5054-5866-8041-e9c9eed9b449" :question/math-academy-id "q-104058" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|-1 & ={1}^{2}+C \\\\ 0-1 & =1+C \\\\ C & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ in implicit form is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104058/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104058"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
